      DRC_TOTAL=0 -> the pre-routing placement is clean, so 100% of the violations
      are router-introduced. (Baseline/categorization runs do not consume budget.)
  [D-attribute] Attributed via routes.json (exact coordinate match, not label
      proximity) and cross-checked against GDS layer-69 polygons. Diagnosed as a
      SAME-NET notch: landing-stub bottom (-190.9973) vs met3<->met2 via pad top
      (-191.1199) = 0.1227um gap. Keepouts checked first: only XC0 declares one
      (1.2um), ~15um away -- not breached.
  [D-knob-probe] Established that every non-pitch knob is a no-op here, because
      route_nets.py's penalty() exempts a net's own metal. 9 knob settings tried,
      all left the violation unchanged. Cheap geometric screen (validated to
      reproduce Magic's result exactly) used to rank candidates without spending
      DRC budget.
  [D-iter-1] Re-ran route_nets.py with the SOLE change --track-multiplier 1.0 -> 1.04
      (pitch 0.7200 -> 0.7488um). Real Magic DRC: 0 violations. Bbox/polygon guard
      confirms the 0 is real. => DRC gate CLOSED after 1 fix iteration.

LVS phase
